\chapter{What we depend on}
\label{Schema}

The extractors read attributes and relationships whose names FBF chose and
may change.
This chapter keeps those dependencies explicit, for three uses.
\begin{description}
\item[At run time] an extractor reads a name through [[attribute]] or
  [[relationship]], which raise [[SchemaError]] when the name is missing.
  A rename then fails with \enquote{comments: no attribute 'body'} rather
  than a [[KeyError]] deep in the code, or worse, an empty column.
\item[In a diff] [[fbf har-diff]] marks the removed names that we depend
  on, which separates the changes that break us from the ones that do not.
\item[In the live tests] each declared name is checked against FBF.
\end{description}

The declaration is the set [[REQUIRED]] of shape records, in the format of
\cref{HAR}: [[type comments attribute body]].
Using the shape's own format makes the comparison with a diff a set
intersection.
Each extractor declares its names in its own chapter, next to the code that
reads them, with [[requires]] in a chunk [[<<required names>>]]; the
build tangles those chunks from all chapters into this module.
Since tangling from several files joins all chunks of the same name, this
module's code goes in [[<<schema functions>>]], not in the
[[<<functions>>]] that every chapter has.

<<[[schema.py]]>>=
"""The FeedbackFruits names that fbf depends on, and checked access."""

REQUIRED = set()

